 "stimulus_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"2\">\n  <li>Here are the graphs of <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2\">f(x)=x^2</span>, <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2−5\">f(x)=x^2−5</span>, and <span data-math=\"f(x)=(x+2)^2−8\">f(x)=(x+2)^2−8</span>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><img height=\"219\" src=\"exercises/media/352f08c5ae18a220.svg\" width=\"272\" alt=\"Line graph: Cost (in $) vs k-th node for three algorithms. Algorithm B (solid black) has the lowest cost, followed by Algorithm A+B (dashed blue), and Algorithm A+B+C (dashed green) has the highest. Costs decrease as k-th node increases. Node C is marked on A+B+C.\"></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 669197,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" type=\"a\">\n  <li>How do the three graphs compare?</li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1334091,
     "content_html": "All three graphs contain the point <span data-math=\"(0,0)\">(0,0)</span>."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334092,
     "content_html": "They all have a negative a coefficient in the vertex form of the equation."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334093,
     "content_html": "The shape is the same but they are in different locations."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334094,
     "content_html": "They all have the same vertex."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 669198,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"2\" type=\"a\">\n  <li>Compare the graphs of <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2\">f(x)=x^2</span> and <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2−5\">f(x)=x^2−5</span>. What role does the <span data-math=\"-5\">-5</span> play in the comparison?</li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1334095,
     "content_html": "Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 5 units."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334096,
     "content_html": "Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph up by 5 units."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334097,
     "content_html": "Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph right by 5 units."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334098,
     "content_html": "Subtracting 5 from the squared term shifts the graph left by 5 units."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 669199,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"3\" type=\"a\">\n  <li>Compare the graphs of <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2\">f(x)=x^2</span> and <span data-math=\"f(x)=(x+2)^2−8\">f(x)=(x+2)^2−8</span>. What roles do the <span data-math=\"+2\">+2</span> and <span data-math=\"-8\">-8</span> play in the comparison?</li>\n  </ol>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1334099,
     "content_html": "Adding 2 to <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> before squaring shifts the graph of <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2\">f(x)=x^2</span> to the down by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph right by 8 units."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334100,
     "content_html": "Adding 2 to <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> before squaring shifts the graph of <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2\">f(x)=x^2</span> to the right by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph up by 8 units."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334101,
     "content_html": "Adding 2 to <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> before squaring shifts the graph of <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2\">f(x)=x^2</span> to the up by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph left by 8 units."
    },
    {
     "id": 1334102,
     "content_html": "Adding 2 to <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> before squaring shifts the graph of <span data-math=\"f(x)=x^2\">f(x)=x^2</span> to the left by 2 units and subtracting 8 from the squared term shifts the graph down by 8 units."
    }
   ],
